<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sebastian of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sebastião I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sebastian of Portugal (Sebastião I) was King of Portugal from 1557 until 1578. He led an invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> that ended in disaster at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alcacer-quibir">Battle of Alcácer Quibir</a> in 1578, where he was killed and his army destroyed by Saadi forces. His death without an heir led to a succession crisis and the union of the Portuguese and Spanish crowns in 1580.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sebastian-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Sebastian of Portugal" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cristóvão de Morais · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebasti%C3%A3o_de_Portugal,_c._1571-1574_-_Crist%C3%B3v%C3%A3o_de_Morais_(Google_Art_Project).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
